        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus endeth the fifteenth year of the reign of the judges over the people of Nephi;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 28:7",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And this is the account of Ammon and his brethren, their journeyings in the land of Nephi, their sufferings in the land, their sorrows, and their afflictions, and their incomprehensible joy, and the reception and safety of the brethren in the land of Jershon. And now may the Lord, the Redeemer of all men, bless their souls forever.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "IE the account covered in Alma 17–28."
          },
          {
            "start": 169,
            "end": 185,
            "text": "Alma 27:18 (16–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 28:8",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And this is the account of the wars and contentions among the Nephites, and also the wars between the Nephites and the Lamanites; and the fifteenth year of the reign of the judges is ended.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 28:9",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And from the first year to the fifteenth has brought to pass the destruction of many thousand lives; yea, it has brought to pass an awful scene of bloodshed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "IE the years recounted in Alma 1–28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 28:10",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 28,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And the bodies of many thousands are laid low in the earth, while the bodies of many thousands are moldering in heaps upon the face of the earth; yea, and many thousands are mourning for the loss of their kindred, because they have reason to fear, according to the promises of the Lord, that they are consigned to a state of endless wo.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "Alma 16:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 174,
            "end": 182,
            "text": "Alma 48:23; D&C 42:45."
